CHANGED (CC BY 4.0 asks that changes are marked):
  trx/screen_matrix.v           his screen_matrix.v with one line changed: row 2 reads " 8 HARDWARE MANDEL ENGINES" instead of "20 ..." (this partition has 8 engines; the
                                TODO in his file asks for the actual count). rtl/screen_matrix.v.diff is the difference. This is the file that is built.
  trx/pixel_gen_mandelbrot.sv   his engine, pipelined: his single clock (two 25 x 25 products, the 50 bit sum, the compare and the update of z in one path) missed 100 MHz by 2.3 ns on the
                                XC7A50T. Now three registered stages and two pixels per engine take turns in the loop (an iteration of one pixel every second clock, one of the engine every clock);
                                the escape decision of an iteration is made one clock later, off the loop. The arithmetic, the add_u50_carry4 module and the result per pixel (iter8) are his.
                                rtl/pixel_gen_mandelbrot.sv.diff is the difference. This is the file that is built.
  trx/fb_scanline_writer.sv     his scheduler with the engines' two pixel contexts: it keeps its bookkeeping for NCORES * 2 pixels and instantiates NCORES engines of the file above;
                                otherwise as he wrote it. rtl/fb_scanline_writer.sv.diff is the difference. This is the file that is built.
  mem/palette_rgb565_256.hex    made by tools/ddt_palette.py from the RGB colours his palette_yuv_256.hex was converted from (named in its line comments); the tool checks
                                his YUV words against those colours. Replaces palette_rom_256x28.sv.

NOT here, on purpose: top.v, video_timing.v, mandel_video_pattern.v, clock_gen_rmii_to_13m5.v, palette_rom_256x28.sv, debounce_btn.sv, c64_font_rom.sv (below), build.tcl, report_dsp_usage.tcl, the Vivado project (their analogue video back end, the MMCM and the
board pins are replaced by trx/); c64_chargen_ucg.hex and c64_font_rom.sv (the C64 character ROM is Commodore's and never goes into this repository, a bench, a package or a
.cor; trx/c64_font_rom.v reads Gideon's overlay font that the host already carries, host/mem/ovl_font8.mem); C64U.xdc (Gideon's pin constraints); the .bit files, the video and the
images of his repository.

What is ours (GPL v3, as the rest of this repository): layer2_ddt_mandel.v, trx/ (ddt_regs.v, ddt_dots.v, ddt_pixw.v, ddt_palette.v, ddt_mandel_core.v, ddt_mandel_video.v,
c64_font_rom.v, ddt_clk_load.v) and sim/. ddt_mandel_core.v contains blocks of his top.v as he wrote them (marked "top.v" in the file); ddt_mandel_video.v contains the palette
rotation, the palette index and the text overlay of his mandel_video_pattern.v as he wrote them.

